DriveSync on Sparky Stereo OS
=============================

Signing in to Google
--------------------

DriveSync signs in with an OAuth client registered with Google by whoever
distributes it. Its author's Flatpak carries his own client; this package
carries none, so until one is provided the window says:

    Google sign-in is not configured for this installation.

DriveSync reads the client from /usr/share/drivesync/oauth.json (the JSON file
Google's console gives for a Desktop client, "installed" section), or from the
file named by the DRIVESYNC_GOOGLE_OAUTH_FILE environment variable.

Credentials
-----------

Tokens are kept by the desktop's Secret Service (KDE Wallet or GNOME Keyring),
never in a file. When the Secret Service is unavailable or locked, DriveSync
says "Secure credential storage is unavailable. Unlock your keyring and try
again." and stores nothing.

What this build adds
--------------------

- A system tray entry (StatusNotifierItem) with Open DriveSync and Quit; with a
  tray, closing the window keeps DriveSync there.
- Plasma notifications when a run finishes with changes, when an item fails and
  when a file changed on both sides.
- On a metered connection synchronization waits and says so; Preferences >
  Background > "Synchronize on Metered Connections" changes that.
- The account menu's "Add local folder to Places" adds the synchronized folder
  to Dolphin's Places and every KDE file dialog.

